   "explain": "Darwin's friends the geologist and the botanist, <b>Charles Lyell</b> and <b>Joseph Hooker</b>, organised a joint presentation at the Linnean Society of London on <b>1 July 1858</b> with the writings of Darwin and Wallace. Then Darwin quickly finished his book, <i>On the Origin of Species</i>, published on <b>24 November 1859</b>. Wallace always remained an admirer of Darwin and even titled one of his books <i>Darwinism</i>. It is an example of how in science two people can reach the same discovery independently."
