    {
     "label": "📞 Chinese whispers",
     "html": "<p>Remember the game of <b>Chinese whispers</b> (the telephone game)? A sentence passes from mouth to mouth and changes a little each time. After 20 passes it is unrecognisable. DNA is copied from parent to child almost perfectly, but every now and then there is a small \"mistake\" (a <b>mutation</b>). A fundamental difference: in the game the mistakes pile up at random, in evolution the environment acts as the \"referee\" and keeps the versions that work best. With millions of generations, two branches of the same family can become different species.</p>"
    }
